==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|incident|al}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪnsɪˈdɛntəl/|/ɪnsəˈdɛntəl/}}
**{{a|US}} {{IPA|en|[ɪnsɪˈdɛ.ɾ̃əl]|[ɪnsɪˈdɛn.tʰəl]|qual1=[[w:flapping|nasal flap]]|qual2=enunciated}}
*** {{audio|en|en-US incidental (enunciated).ogg|Audio (US; enunciated)}}
*** {{audio|en|en-US incidental (nasal flapping).ogg|Audio (US; more common realization)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Loosely [[associated#Adjective|associated]]; of limited [[relevant#Adjective|relevance]] except [[indirect#Adjective|indirectly]]; only {{l|en|accident|id=philosophical sense, versus essence or substance|accidentally}} related.
#: {{ux|en|That character, though colorful, is '''incidental''' to the overall plot.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''incidental''' evidence}}
# Existing [[tangential]]ly, being a [[byproduct]], a [[tangent]], or a likely [[consequence]].
#: {{ux|en|Injuries are '''incidental''' to contact sports: they're going to happen.}}
# Occurring by chance.
# {{lb|en|physics|of radiation}} Entering or approaching, prior to [[reflection]] (more frequently [[incident]]).

